{
  "_": [
    "Rung 1 of the fleet ladder: two real instances, text only.",
    "A creates a server, A copies the invite, B joins by it, each sends a",
    "message and the OTHER one has to see it. Then A deletes the server and",
    "both of them have to lose it.",
    "",
    "Nothing here is provable by one instance. The Rust harness proves the ops",
    "converge; this proves the widgets agree - the member panel, the channel",
    "list, the message row and the server strip all showing what the CRDT says.",
    "",
    "The server is created by this run and deleted by its cleanup, which runs",
    "even when the run fails. These are real identities on the real relay, so",
    "that discipline is not optional.",
    "",
    "${RUN} is unique per run and belongs in every message: the relay holds",
    "undelivered traffic for three days and these identities are stable, so a",
    "fixed string can be matched by an earlier run's message.",
    "",
    "run: powershell -File scripts/fleet.ps1 -Scenario server_invite_message"
  ],
  "peers": ["a", "b"],
  "steps": [
    { "peer": "all", "op": "wait_for", "target": "text:Connected", "timeout_ms": 120000 },

    { "peer": "a", "op": "tap", "target": "semantics:Create a server" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "enter_text", "target": "hint:My Awesome Server", "value": "fleet-probe" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "tap", "target": "text:Create", "index": 0 },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "wait_for", "target": "server:fleet-probe", "timeout_ms": 30000 },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "open_server", "name": "fleet-probe" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "wait_for", "target": "channel:general", "timeout_ms": 30000 },

    { "peer": "a", "op": "right_click", "target": "server:fleet-probe" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "tap", "target": "menu > text:Invite people" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "wait_for", "target": "type:SelectableText", "timeout_ms": 20000 },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "capture", "target": "type:SelectableText", "as": "INVITE" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "key", "value": "escape" },

    { "peer": "b", "op": "tap", "target": "semantics:Create a server" },
    { "peer": "b", "op": "enter_text", "target": "hint:Invite link or server ID", "value": "${INVITE}" },
    { "peer": "b", "op": "tap", "target": "text:Join", "index": 0 },
    { "peer": "b", "op": "wait_for", "target": "server:fleet-probe", "timeout_ms": 90000 },
    { "peer": "b", "op": "open_server", "name": "fleet-probe" },
    { "peer": "b", "op": "open_channel", "name": "general" },

    { "peer": "a", "op": "log", "message": "the member panel has to show B, not just the CRDT" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "wait_for", "target": "text:probe-b", "timeout_ms": 60000 },

    { "peer": "a", "op": "open_channel", "name": "general" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "enter_text", "target": "field", "value": "hello from a ${RUN}" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "key", "value": "enter" },
    { "peer": "b", "op": "wait_for", "target": "text:hello from a ${RUN}", "timeout_ms": 60000 },

    { "peer": "b", "op": "enter_text", "target": "field", "value": "hello back from b ${RUN}" },
    { "peer": "b", "op": "key", "value": "enter" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "wait_for", "target": "text:hello back from b ${RUN}", "timeout_ms": 60000 },

    { "peer": "a", "op": "log", "message": "one row per message, not two: the optimistic write and the one that arrives must reconcile" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "expect_count", "target": "text:hello from a ${RUN}", "value": 1 },
    { "peer": "b", "op": "expect_count", "target": "text:hello from a ${RUN}", "value": 1 },

    { "peer": "all", "op": "dump", "name": "converged" }
  ],
  "cleanup": [
    { "peer": "a", "op": "right_click", "target": "server:fleet-probe" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "tap", "target": "menu > text:Server settings" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "tap", "target": "text:Danger", "index": 0 },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "tap", "target": "text:Delete server", "index": 0 },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "log", "message": "index 1: index 0 is the dialog's TITLE, and tapping a title silently does nothing" },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "tap", "target": "dialog > text:Delete server", "index": 1 },
    { "peer": "a", "op": "wait_for", "gone": "server:fleet-probe", "timeout_ms": 30000 },
    { "peer": "b", "op": "log", "message": "the delete tombstone has to reach B's server strip too" },
    { "peer": "b", "op": "wait_for", "gone": "server:fleet-probe", "timeout_ms": 90000 }
  ]
}
